'''Muntatge Automobilístic de Balboa, S.A.''' (MAB) is a Balboan {{w|completely knocked down|CKD}} vehicle assembly company based in the [[Portnou]]. The company assembles electric and plug-in hybrid vehicles from imported kits under contract for multiple international brands, primarily serving the domestic market and the [[BTPMEU]] tariff area. It is listed on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] under the ticker MAB and is a constituent of the [[SCX 100]] index.

MAB was founded in 2008 by Xavier Camps i Rovira, a former operations manager at [[Yonezawa Balboa]], who identified that several electric vehicle manufacturers — particularly [[SKQ]] and [[Vidal]] — lacked assembly capacity within the BTPMEU and were importing fully built vehicles at higher tariff rates. MAB positioned itself as a multi-brand CKD assembler, offering assembly services to any manufacturer seeking BTPMEU tariff qualification.

The company assembles approximately 12,000 vehicles per year across its contract brands, with SKQ entry-level electric vehicles accounting for the majority of output. MAB's facility in the Sant Cristòfor Free Trade Zone performs body welding, painting, and final assembly from imported kits. Approximately 65 per cent of output is sold domestically, with the remainder exported to BTPMEU member states.

